Distribution revision: 2026-10-23.
This source distribution removes personal and deployment documentation and
replaces it with independent build and validation instructions. Test-runner
names and a verifier User-Agent are neutralized. Recording behavior, package
identifiers, dependency versions and protocol trust anchors are retained.

Original license and attribution notices are preserved. The Gradle wrapper
scripts retain their original-author and Apache License 2.0 notices verbatim;
the wrapper JAR is unchanged. Dependencies retain their upstream licensing.
This notice does not replace the licenses of upstream components.

Distribution revision 0.3 improves Serbian interface wording and removes
organizer-specific instructions from individual-edition recovery messages.

Distribution revision 0.4 simplifies individual setup, recommends the Android
folder picker, offers battery settings before recording, and changes fresh-install
defaults to evidence mode, playable uploads and ordinary network connections.
Saved privacy choices and existing queued-file policies are retained.

Distribution revision 0.4.1 retains Stop during recovery, adds a notification
Stop action and scopes idle-camera callbacks to their own capture sessions.
PIN verification now runs off the UI thread with visible progress, serialized
security decisions, and uncancelled rate-limit/wipe side effects. Recording
controls show state colors and progress independently of upload status queries.

Distribution revision 0.4.2 isolates recovery failures by journal, retains
unresolved evidence while allowing new independent recordings, and serializes
recovery and capture ownership. Recovery support codes contain no file/account data.

Distribution revision 0.4.3 adds a bounded two-transfer delivery pipeline with
single-transfer fallback after failures or sustained throughput loss. Queue
ownership, folder setup and token refresh are serialized where necessary.
Recording quality settings, evidence proofs and destination policies are unchanged.

Distribution revision 0.4.4 replaces repeated SAF child-name queries with a
single projected lookup, retains complete read-back verification, rejects partial
cloud listings, and stores encrypted numeric-only timing totals for diagnosis.

Distribution revision 0.4.5 expands the camera preview to the screen width,
preserves its aspect ratio, and keeps recording controls visible while scrolling.
Recording, encoding and upload behavior are unchanged from revision 0.4.4.

Distribution revision 0.4.6 puts Settings in a fixed header and outlined flash
and audio toggles over the camera preview, with accessible state/action labels.
Audio track selection remains fixed during recording. Capture and delivery
implementation remains unchanged from revision 0.4.5.

Distribution revision 0.4.7 presents audio selection as a labeled checkbox
below the camera viewport, visible without scrolling, while retaining the
fixed Settings icon and camera flash overlay. Capture and delivery code is unchanged.
